3. The nesting and scheduling problems
The rationale of this section is to map the research structure of nesting and scheduling problems in AM, and thus, responding to RQ1. In this study, the analysis extends conventional qualitative reviews, as we leverage the qualitative study through two well-accepted bibliometric methods - conceptual analysis (Aria and Cuccurullo, 2017) and main path analysis (De Nooy et al., 2018). Conceptual analysis is utilized to connect the fundamental concepts of the research field (Zupic and Cˇater, 2015). Specifically, it can be used to address the different decision types of the nesting and scheduling problem and its related problems. The main path reveals connections among core papers, providing significant details on the relative influence of the publications (De Nooy et al., 2018).

